# Cloudflare Pages SPA fallback (production = https://mybishbash.app).
# Real static files (launcher pages, /assets, /icons, manifest, and the
# per-route index.html files the build now emits) are served directly — Pages
# matches an existing asset before applying this rule.
#
# Verified 2026-09-04 (MBB-6): this rule alone does NOT make deep links return
# 200. With it live on main, https://mybishbash.app/privacy still answered
# HTTP 404 — dist/404.html wins over the rewrite, so the body rendered but the
# status stayed 404 and crawlers dropped the page. The fix is the prerendered
# <route>/index.html files (vite.config.js routePrerenderPlugin). This rule is
# kept as a belt-and-braces fallback for dynamic paths (/card/:id,
# /intercept/:launcher) that cannot be prerendered.
/*    /index.html    200
